# Default: treat everything as text, normalized to LF in the repository
# and on checkout. Windows checkouts of this repo (core.autocrlf=true)
# would otherwise reintroduce CRLF into files with no explicit override --
# confirmed to break a Linux container's #!/bin/bash shebang in
# entrypoint.sh, and to corrupt content-hash provenance checks on HTML/JS/
# JSON files recovered in DEPLOY-GOV-2E. LF is this repository's canonical
# line-ending policy for all text content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary markers -- never run text normalization or diff on these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.wav binary
*.woff binary
*.eot binary
*.ttf binary
*.svg binary

sgf_engine/VENDORED_FROM.txt text eol=lf

# Windows-native launcher exception to the repo-wide eol=lf policy above.
# cmd.exe's batch parser is byte-oriented and codepage-dependent; a
# real Owner test on Windows 10 confirmed that LF-only .cmd content
# (silently produced by the blanket eol=lf rule above, regardless of
# what line endings were written at commit time) corrupts line/token
# parsing -- see E10-Z1-AUDIO-PRODUCTION-001 and
# tests/test_e10_zone1_audio_launcher_windows_compat.py. Every Owner
# launcher under tools/e10_zone1_audio/ (Set A, Set B, and any future
# set) must always check out with CRLF, on every platform, or the
# launcher breaks again. Glob covers current and future Run_Audition_*
# launchers so this exception doesn't need a new line added by hand
# each time a new set is created.
tools/e10_zone1_audio/Run_Audition_Set_*.cmd text eol=crlf
tools/e10_zone1_audio/Run_Audition_Set_*.ps1 text eol=crlf
